From d38be16c1658564da75d53f63a2319e8e950fdfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:59:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp2: Add the IMX415

Add the IMX415 to the rkisp2 IPA. The sensor helper provides the black
level of 0x32 at 10 bits from the data sheet, which the kernel driver
programs as the default BLKLEVEL, so that the IPAs subtract it without
a tuning file entry. The tuning file uses auto exposure, grey world
white balance, black level subtraction, gamma and colour space
conversion, and the libipa defaults for the AGC targets, a mean of 0.16
and a lower bound of 0.5 on the highlights. The colour correction
matrices, the colour temperature gain curve and the white balance modes
are converted from the Raspberry Pi tuning file of the IMX415, which
describes the sensor and is not specific to a camera board. There is no
lens shading calibration yet.

The exposure and gain written to the IMX415 at the start of a frame take
effect in the next frame. With a delay of two frames the IPA believed
the values to be in effect one frame later than they are, and the AGC
regulated on a luminance that does not correspond to the exposure it
accounted for. Measured on an RV1126 with the rkisp2 pipeline, which
writes the controls when the VICAP completes the previous frame, the
measured luminance follows a change of exposure or gain one frame before
the frame the metadata reports it for. The blanking delays are left as
they are, they were not measured.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp       |  2 +
 src/ipa/rkisp2/data/imx415.yaml               | 84 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/ipa/rkisp2/data/meson.build               |  1 +
 .../sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp       |  4 +-
 4 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/ipa/rkisp2/data/imx415.yaml

--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -622,6 +622,8 @@ class CameraSensorHelperImx415 : public
 public:
 	CameraSensorHelperImx415()
 	{
+		/* From datasheet: 0x32 at 10bits. */
+		blackLevel_ = 3200;
 		gain_ = AnalogueGainExp{ 1.0, expGainDb(0.3) };
 	}
 };
